&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated as deemed distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $20.2&amp;#160;million in 2025&amp;#160;and $13.3 million in 2024&amp;#160;and was included within Other Paid&amp;#160;In&amp;#160;Capital in the Comparative Balance Sheet. We will make all necessary adjustments to account balances upon a ruling in Docket No. AC18-220-000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the United States enacted the "Tax Cuts and Jobs Act" (TCJA). The changes in the TCJA are effective for taxation years beginning after December 31, 2017. While the changes are broad and complex, the most significant change is the reduction in the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. We recorded a $89.4 million decrease to our 2017 deferred income tax liability, a $29.1 million increase to our 2017 deferred income tax&amp;#160;asset&amp;#160;and an offsetting increase of $118.5 million to our regulatory liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;In 2018 pursuant to guidance established in FERC Docket No. PL19-2-000, we began amortizing the regulated liability utilizing the reverse South Georgia flowback methodology over the&amp;#160;27.7 year&amp;#160;remaining life of the assets. In 2025, we recorded a $4.3 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $1.1&amp;#160;million decrease to our 2025&amp;#160;deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $3.2&amp;#160;million benefit to our 2025&amp;#160;deferred federal tax expense. In 2024, we recorded a $4.3 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $1.0 million decrease to our 2024&amp;#160;deferred income tax&amp;#160;asset&amp;#160;and an offsetting $3.3 million benefit to our 2024&amp;#160;deferred federal tax expense. In 2021,&amp;#160;as a result of&amp;#160;the East Tennessee Stipulation and Agreement Docket RP20-980, we established a deficient deferred income tax (DDIT) regulatory asset with an initial balance of $32.7 million which is to be amortized over 5.25 years beginning on January 1, 2021. In 2025, we recorded a $6.2 million decrease to the DDIT regulatory asset and an offsetting $6.2 million expense to our 2025&amp;#160;deferred federal tax expense. In 2024, we recorded a $6.2 million decrease to the DDIT regulatory asset and an offsetting $6.2 million expense to our 2024&amp;#160;deferred federal tax expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: normal; margin: 0in 0in 0in 13.5pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;10. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;In the normal course of business, Enbridge and its affiliates perform centralized corporate functions for us, including legal, accounting, compliance, treasury and other areas. Enbridge and its affiliates charge such expenses based on the cost of actual services provided or using various allocation methodologies based on our percentage of assets, earnings or other measures, as compared to Enbridge's other affiliates. Advances payable - affiliates do not bear interest. Advances are&amp;#160;carried out&amp;#160;as unsecured, open accounts and are segregated between current and non-current amounts. Increases and decreases in advances generally result from the movement of funds to provide for our operations, capital expenditures and debt payments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Our transactions with related parties are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -13.5pt; line-height: normal; margin: 0in 0in 0in 13.5pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class="MsoNormalTable" style="margin-left: 26.5pt; border-image: initial; border: medium none currentcolor;" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; height: 22.9pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 304.45pt; border: solid black 1.0pt; border-bottom: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid black .75pt; mso-border-left-alt: solid black .75pt; mso-border-right-alt: solid black .75pt; padding: 0in 5.05pt 0in 5.05pt; height: 22.9pt;" colspan="6" width="406"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;Statement of Income (in millions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="mso-yfti-irow: 1; height: 17.5pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 146.95pt; border: none; border-left: solid black 1.0pt; mso-border-left-alt: solid black .75pt; padding: 0in 5.4pt 0in 5.05pt; height: 17.5pt;" valign="top" width="196"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
