                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The July 18, 2018 Commission order in Docket No. PL17-1-001 provided guidance regarding the Commission&#8217;s income tax allowance policy for pipelines owned by master limited partnerships and the related deferred tax balances, including balances in Account 282 (Accumulated Deferred Taxes-Other). The July 18 Order explained that MLP pipelines could elect to eliminate certain deferred tax balances. East Tennessee&#8217;s parent company, Spectra Energy Partners, LP, has a pending request with the FERC Chief Accountant to eliminate amounts recorded in Account 282, including amounts in Account 282 for East Tennessee. Certain amounts in Account 282 may be excluded in the development of jurisdictional recourse rates in the future</span>
